CloudBurrow patch 88 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1458). Applies after patch 0080; needs patches
0030 and 0056.

Patches 0030 and 0056 give a table made by CREATE TABLE, with a column
list or AS SELECT, the pseudo-column _PARTITION_STREAMED, the time
CloudBurrow's front streamed a row, which DML reads to refuse a row
streamed in the last 30 minutes ("within the last 30 minutes",
https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/data-manipulation-language); not
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS, which may name a table there without it, so
a table that statement made held its streamed rows from DML only while
in the streaming buffer (measured through the front: a DELETE of a row
streamed a minute before ran). It now gets the column when the statement
makes the table (no SQLite table of that name), with a column list or AS
SELECT, NULL on the SELECT's rows; a table that is there is left as it
is, and so is a temporary table. ctas_streamed_at_column_test.go fails
without the patch and passes with it.

